# Runner safety

AI is **proposer**; human or explicit job flag is **approver**. `main` / `master` are **protected**.

## Allowed (default)

- Create feature branch (`ai/job-*`, `feat/*`, etc.)
- Edit code on that branch
- Run tests and linters
- Commit **only** when user or job payload says `commit: true` / equivalent
- Open PR when job allows

## Forbidden without explicit approval

- Push to `main` / `master`
- Merge to protected branches
- `git push --force` on shared branches
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`) unless user requests
- Destructive DB migrations, mass file delete, `.env` / secrets edits
- Major dependency upgrades
- Destructive NovelGuard file moves without dry-run preview + approval

## Git discipline

- Never update git config for the user.
- Prefer new commits over amend unless user requested amend and HEAD is unpushed local work.
- Do not commit cache dirs, `.env`, or credentials.

## Headless / queued jobs

- Start from updated `main`; work only on job branch.
- Unless instructed: **no commit** — return diff summary and verification results.
- One concurrent mutating job per repo (respect external lock files).

## NovelGuard product safety

- Duplicate detection must not use log/report artifacts as inputs unless spec says so.
- File cleanup/moves: dry-run first; apply only after approval.
